:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKOBJ/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKOBJ/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.Up to 14 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJOPR:EPK.
:PD.Object operational authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*DLT:EPK.
:PD.Delete authority.
:PT.:PK.*EXECUTE:EPK.
:PD.Execute authority.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:PT.:PK.*UPD:EPK.
:PD.Update authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTLMGT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CLRLIB.Clear Library (CLRLIB)
:P.Use the Clear Library (CLRLIB) command to delete every object in a
library, keeping the library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLRLIB/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLRLIB/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALLAVL:EPK.
:PD.Every available ASP device.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYLIB.Copy Library (CPYLIB)
:P.Use the Copy Library (CPYLIB) command to copy a library and its
objects to another library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYLIB/FROMLIB'.From library (FROMLIB)
:P.The from library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYLIB/TOLIB'.To library (TOLIB)
:P.The to library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYLIB/CRTLIB'.Create library (CRTLIB)
:P.Whether to create library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYLIB/TOASP'.To ASP number (TOASP)
:P.The to ASP number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYLIB/TOASPDEV'.To ASP device (TOASPDEV)
:P.The to ASP device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ASP, *ASPGRPPRI.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTDTAARA.Create Data Area (CRTDTAARA)
:P.Use the Create Data Area (CRTDTAARA) command to create a data area,
local or DDM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/DTAARA'.Data area (DTAARA)
:P.The data area, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/TYPE'.Type (TYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEC:EPK.
:PD.Decimal.
:PT.:PK.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*DDM:EPK.
:PD.DDM.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LGL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/LEN'.Length (LEN)
:P.The length for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2000.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Decimal positions
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/VALUE'.Initial value (VALUE)
:P.The initial value for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.hexadecimal-value:EPV.
:PD.Type the value as characters or as hexadecimal digits in X'...'.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/RMTDTAARA'.Remote data area (RMTDTAARA)
:P.The remote data area for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
:P.The remote location name of the system at the other end of the
connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/DEV'.APPC device (DEV)
:P.The APPC device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/LCLLOCNAME'.Local location (LCLLOCNAME)
:P.The local location name this system uses on the connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/MODE'.Mode (MODE)
:P.The mode for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/RMTNETID'.Remote network identifier (RMTNETID)
:P.The network identifier of the remote location.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAARA/RDB'.Relational database (RDB)
:P.The relational database for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 18 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTDTAQ.Create Data Queue (CRTDTAQ)
:P.Use the Create Data Queue (CRTDTAQ) command to create a data queue,
standard or DDM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/DTAQ'.Data queue (DTAQ)
:P.The data queue, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/TYPE'.Type (TYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PK.*DDM:EPK.
:PD.DDM.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/MAXLEN'.Maximum entry length (MAXLEN)
:P.The maximum entry length for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 64512.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/FORCE'.Force to auxiliary storage (FORCE)
:P.Whether to force to auxiliary storage.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/SEQ'.Sequence (SEQ)
:P.The sequence for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIFO:EPK.
:PD.First in, first out.
:PT.:PK.*KEYED:EPK.
:PD.Keyed.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIFO.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/KEYLEN'.Key length (KEYLEN)
:P.The key length for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 256.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/SENDERID'.Include sender ID (SENDERID)
:P.Whether to include sender ID.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/SIZE'.Queue size (SIZE)
:P.The queue size for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Maximum number of entries
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777216.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MAX16MB, *MAX2GB.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Initial number of entries
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777216.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 16 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/AUTORCL'.Automatic reclaim (AUTORCL)
:P.Whether to automatic reclaim.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/RMTDTAQ'.Remote data queue (RMTDTAQ)
:P.The remote data queue for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
:P.The remote location name of the system at the other end of the
connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/DEV'.APPC device (DEV)
:P.The APPC device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDTAQ/LCLLOCNAME'.Local location (LCLLOCNAME)
:P.The local location name this system uses on the connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
