:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLIB/CRTOBJAUD'.Auditing for new objects (CRTOBJAUD)
:P.The auditing value given to objects created in the library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLCOBJ.Deallocate Object (DLCOBJ)
:P.Use the Deallocate Object (DLCOBJ) command to release locks the job
holds.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLCOBJ/OBJ'.Object specifications (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
