:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNMOBJ/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVDTAARA.Retrieve Data Area (RTVDTAARA)
:P.Use the Retrieve Data Area (RTVDTAARA) command to copy all or part of
a data area into a CL variable.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVDTAARA/DTAARA'.Data area specification (DTAARA)
:P.The data area, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Data area
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Substring
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Start position
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2000.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVDTAARA/RTNVAR'.CL var for returned value (RTNVAR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of returned value. Give a
character variable of at least 2000 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKF.Work with Files (WRKF)
:P.Use the Work with Files (WRKF) command to show a list of files and
work with them through options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKF/FILEATR'.File attributes (FILEATR)
:P.The file attributes for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*LF:EPK.
:PD.Line feed.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PK.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BSCF, *CMNF, *DDMF, *DSPF, *ICFF, *MXDF, *PF,
*PRTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKLIB.Work with Libraries (WRKLIB)
:P.Use the Work with Libraries (WRKLIB) command to show a list of
libraries and work with them through options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLIB/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLIB/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLIB/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALLAVL:EPK.
:PD.Every available ASP device.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOBJ.Work with Objects (WRKOBJ)
:P.Use the Work with Objects (WRKOBJ) command to show a list of objects
and work with them through options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJ/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALLAVL:EPK.
:PD.Every available ASP device.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLUSRAVL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJ/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.Up to 110 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
